From 303290d306e0484e8f4b80c756e4555040fdcab2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:56:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Finish the op list: 539 ops, none of them dead

Battery group 56 walks the 284 placed locs, reads every op1-op5 off poh.loc
and poh_templates.loc, and fails if one of them has no trigger anywhere. It
is the other direction from check 39, which has caught triggers on ops a loc
does not carry since the furniture round; this is the one that was never
checked. An op the loc DOES carry with no trigger is a click that does
nothing, and a click that does nothing is indistinguishable from a bug. It
found six more than the survey did - op4=Upgrade on four tool stores and two
workbenches that nobody had noticed.

Two of them are real activities. The archery target wants a bow and arrows -
a bow being a worn right-hand weapon with attackrange above 1, the same test
tut_giant_rat uses rather than a list of bows to fall behind - and the
dartboard wants darts. Both spend the BEST ammunition carried, spend it
before the roll so a miss costs something, and pay experience only on a hit.
A shot is three ticks: the target is a thing to build, not a way to train.

The rest are honest, and what is missing is always one of two things. Either
the house is empty - hangman, the mime, the elemental balance, the attack
stone and the dungeon challenge are all things OSRS plays against another
person - or the items are not in a 2006 cache. The clockmaker's bench makes
nine clockwork toys and not one of them is in obj.pack; the heraldry stand
makes steel heraldic helmets, shields and banners and none of those are
either, and the fifteen heraldic kiteshields that DO exist are treasure trail
rewards that making at a stand would undercut.

rs2check 0 ERROR / 0 CHECK; poh_battery ALL PASS (56 groups);
poh_mutate 106/106 caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J1qUhTcu63bJ3hCBBxy7nU
